# OBMC WIRED — selected where C selects it, recon byte-identical to dav1d
#
# commit:  (this change, on top of 59becc5a4 "OBMC is 22 % of blocks at preset 0")
# host:    i265 (Core Ultra 7 265K, 20 threads, 30 GiB, native Linux)
# gate:    rust/tools/obmc_gate.sh
# decoder: dav1d (system)
# cells:   public-domain derf clips, cli_qp 40, 2 frames, flat low-delay P
#
# ## RESULT
#
#     clip     size     preset  OBMC blocks  recon vs dav1d
#     vidyo3   256x256  0       186          2/2
#     vidyo1   256x256  0        76          2/2
#     johnny   256x256  0        12          2/2
#     vidyo3   128x128  0        54          2/2
#     vidyo3   256x256  2         0          2/2
#     vidyo1   256x256  2         0          2/2
#
# Preset 2 codes ZERO, which is `svt_aom_get_obmc_level`'s level-5 arm and
# matches the census exactly: the injection cannot have widened the candidate
# set where C's own ladder closes it.
#
# ## THE BUG THE RECON CHECK CAUGHT, AND NOTHING ELSE WOULD HAVE
#
# First wiring: 180 OBMC blocks selected, stream decodable, and **120 luma
# samples wrong** on vidyo3 256x256 p0 (chroma clean, magnitudes +/-1..3, in a
# band across the OBMC blocks at mi row 8).
#
# Cause: the 4-wide pairing rule in `foreach_overlappable_nb_above`
# (enc_inter_prediction.c:721-726). For a neighbour one mi wide C rewinds
# `above_mi_col` to the start of the pair -- which is what `rel_mi_col`, and so
# the prediction GEOMETRY, uses -- but takes the mode info from the pair's
# SECOND block, `prev_row_mi + above_mi_col + 1`, because that is the half
# carrying chroma. The port's `VisitedNb` recorded only `rel_mi`, so the
# neighbour's MOTION was read from the wrong cell of every 4-wide pair.
#
# `VisitedNb::mi_index` now carries C's index and
# `four_wide_neighbours_are_paired` pins it. After the fix: 0 differing samples
# on both frames of every cell.
#
# This is exactly why the gate asserts RECON against an independent decoder and
# not sizes: the blend depends on the neighbours' motion, which is never
# re-transmitted, so a wrong neighbour is invisible to every byte-count check.
#
# ## MEMORY MODEL — C'S, MEASURED
#
# C allocates the OBMC scratch ONCE per `ModeDecisionContext` (per MD thread),
# sized by SUPERBLOCK, and only when `obmc_allowed` (`md_process.c:374-381`):
#
#     obmc_buff_0 / _1 : sb_size * sb_size * bits * MAX_PLANES   bytes
#     obmc_conv_buf    : sb_size * sb_size                        u16
#
# `obmc_pred_arm::ObmcBuffers` is that, as a thread-local grown on first use,
# pinned by `scratch_is_superblock_sized_and_grown_once`. Nothing in the OBMC
# path allocates per block or per candidate:
#
#   * the two neighbour walks fill a fixed `[VisitedNb; MAX_VISITED_NB]`
#     (C's `nb_max` is at most 4) instead of returning a `Vec`;
#   * the per-neighbour plane geometry fills `[NbPredGeom; MAX_NB_PRED_GEOM]`
#     instead of returning a `Vec` (C builds no list at all -- it predicts
#     inside the loop);
#   * the two mi spans the walks read are projected into fixed arrays.
#
# The `_into` forms are pinned equal to the `Vec` forms they replace by
# `into_walks_match_the_vec_walks` and `geom_into_matches_the_vec_form`, so the
# allocation-free path cannot drift from the transcription it came from.
#
# MEASURED with heaptrack on vidyo3 256x256 p0, 2 frames
# (`CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_DEBUG=line-tables-only`):
#
#     calls to allocation functions : 863,166
#     peak heap memory consumption  : 6.26M
#     allocating frames inside obmc_pred_arm : 0
#
# The zero is the point: the scratch does not appear in the profile at all
# because it is allocated once per thread and reused, which is what makes this
# C's memory model rather than a per-block allocation wearing a thread-local's
# clothes. A regression to per-block buffers would still pass every byte gate,
# which is why the sizing and the reuse are pinned by unit tests.
#
# ## THE MV REFINEMENT (added the same day)
#
# `opt_non_translation_motion_mode_obmc` -> `obmc_motion_refinement` ->
# `single_motion_search` is now wired at the MD stage `obmc_refine_stage`
# selects (stage 1 at refine_level 1/2, stage 3 at 3/4). The search scores
# candidate vectors against `wsrc`/`mask` -- the source with the neighbours'
# predictions blended out (`calc_target_weighted_pred`) -- built once per block
# behind C's `obmc_weighted_pred_ready`, in the same thread-local scratch.
#
# IT CHANGED THE SELECTION, which is the point: 186/76/12/54 OBMC blocks became
# 168/92/14/56 on the four preset-0 cells. Re-pinned with the reason recorded;
# the recon column stayed 2/2 throughout and is the assertion that matters.
#
# AND IT CAUGHT A SECOND BUG THE SAME WAY THE FIRST ONE WAS CAUGHT. The first
# refinement wiring left 653 luma samples diverging from dav1d on vidyo3
# 256x256 p0. Cause: C clears `cand_bf->valid_luma_pred` when the refinement
# CHANGES the MV (product_coding_loop.c:6817), which makes `full_loop_core`
# re-run the prediction; the port has no lazy flag and kept MDS0's. The MV that
# gets CODED is the refined one, so a prediction built from the old MV is one
# no decoder reproduces -- wrong pixels, not a quality difference. The adapter
# now rebuilds luma, chroma AND the blend on a `Refined` outcome, exactly as
# the warp adapter does.
#
# ## WHAT IS STILL NOT WIRED
#
# The INJECTION-time refinement: `obmc_ctrls.refine_level == 0`, which
# `set_obmc_controls` gives only at obmc_level 1, i.e. preset MR. There
# `inj_non_simple_modes` calls `InjectHooks::obmc_motion_refinement` directly
# rather than through an MD stage, and that hook still returns "valid,
# unrefined". Presets 0 and 1 -- where the census measured 22.5 % and 27.0 % of
# blocks -- are at obmc_level 3, refine_level 1, and ARE refined.
#
# `obmc_trans_face_off` is also unwired and inert at the presets that matter:
# `set_obmc_controls` gives `trans_face_off = 0` at levels 1 and 3, i.e. at
# presets MR / 0 / 1, the only band where C selects OBMC at all.
#
# The 10-bit arm is absent: C sizes `obmc_buff_*` for `hbd_md ? 2 : 1` and the
# neighbour predictions would come from the 10-bit DPB twin.
# `bd10_tree_supported` refuses an OBMC leaf, so a 10-bit frame that picks one
# drops back to the u8 output rather than miscoding it.
